From: ms178-3

loop_unroll + vectorize: perfect the complete-unroller's carried-value model
and harden the late vectorizer's reduction-phis, validated against GCC on a
35-kernel adversarial red-team corpus.

loop_unroll.rs
  * Header-phi iteration model (LoopPhiModel): a per-iteration SSA environment
    that substitutes EVERY header phi (IV + all loop-carried values) with the
    value it holds at the entry of that iteration.  This closes three soundness
    holes in the carried-value threading that previously kept such a phi at its
    INIT value in every cloned iteration:
        - constant back value            (first-iteration flag `first = 0`)
        - loop-invariant back value      (`cur = param`)
        - cross-phi back value           (`x = y; y = t`)
  * Header-side-effect modeling in the general cloner: the loop condition's
    own instructions (`cnt++` in `for (i=0; cnt++, i<N; i++)`) run `trip + 1`
    times (the failing evaluation included).  A final-guard block re-runs them
    once more after the last clone and its fresh outputs become the live-out
    values.  Real observable side effects (store / volatile / call) in the
    header make the cloner fail closed (leave the loop rolled).
  * Two-block cloner adopts the same environment model and rejects header
    side effects (it clones only the work blocks, never the header).

vectorize.rs
  * Reject a loop whose reduction has any unhandled loop-carried phi (e.g. a
    `last = a[i]` value whose back-edge incoming is a loop-block Value).  The
    vector transform would leave such a phi on the scaled induction variable
    and silently read A[0], A[8], ... instead of A[i].  Fails closed to the
    scalar form, which is correct.
  * Detect the swapped conditional-sum guard `Select(cond, s, s + x)` (the
    `if (a[i] & 1) continue; s += a[i];` shape) and reject it before the
    masked-widening intrinsic, which only encodes add-when-cond-true.


